module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.AssociatedModule.SmallEtaleFullyFaithful

/-!
# Local bijectivity of the sections comparison on the small étale site

Stacks 070S part (2) asserts that, on the small `τ`-site of a scheme `S`, the associated module
`𝓕^a` of a quasi-coherent `𝒪_S`-module `𝓕` is computed by the sections formula
`(f : T → S) ↦ Γ(T, f^*𝓕)` of Stacks Definition 03DU (4), that is, that the comparison morphism
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.sectionsComparison` is locally bijective.  **This file proves it
locally bijective for `τ = étale`**, and deduces the small étale halves of Stacks 0GN7 and of
Stacks 06VE (1) with no hypothesis.

Both halves of local bijectivity rest on one geometric fact: an open subscheme of an object of
the small étale site of `S` is again an object of that site — the open immersion is étale, so its
composite with an étale structure morphism is étale — and the affine such opens lying over affine
opens of `S` cover.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.openSubObj` and `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.openSubHom`: an
  open of the underlying scheme of an object of the small étale site, as an object of that site,
  and its open immersion.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.affineSubordinateCover` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.affineSubordinateCoverOver`: the covering of an object by those
  of its affine opens which lie over an affine open of `S`, and its refinement subordinate to a
  given open of `S`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.pullbackPresheaf`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.pullbackUnit` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.pullbackUnitSection`: the source of the comparison, the unit of
  the pullback--pushforward adjunction at `𝓕`, and the generators of the source.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.mem_topology_sieve₀_affineSubordinateCover` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.mem_topology_sieve₀_affineSubordinateCoverOver`: those affine
  opens cover, for the small étale topology.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.surjective_app_sectionsComparison`: the comparison is surjective
  over an object which is affine and lies over an affine open of `S`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isLocallySurjective_sectionsComparison`: **the comparison is
  locally surjective for the small étale topology**, half of Stacks 070S (2).
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.exists_mem_span_pullbackUnitSection`: every section of the
  pullback is a combination of generators indexed by a single open of `S`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isLocallyInjective_sectionsComparison`: **the comparison is
  locally injective for the small étale topology**, the other half.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.sectionsComparisonSheafifiesToIso`: **Stacks 070S (2) for
  `S_étale`**, i.e. `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.SectionsComparisonSheafifiesToIso` with no
  hypothesis.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.sectionsSheafOfModules'`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.associatedModuleIsoSectionsSheafOfModules'` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.associatedModuleObjIsoSections`: **the sections description of
  `𝓕^a`**, the identification of the associated module with the sections sheaf
  `(f : T → S) ↦ Γ(T, f^*𝓕)` that Stacks Definition 03DU (4) names it by, and its reading at a
  single object of the site.  The two primed names are the same objects as
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.sectionsSheafOfModules` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.associatedModuleIsoSectionsSheafOfModules`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.unitIsoOnQuasicoherent`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.full_associatedModuleQcoh'`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.faithful_associatedModuleQcoh'` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.fullyFaithfulAssociatedModuleQcoh'`: **the small étale half of
  Stacks 0GN7 and of Stacks 06VE (1), with no hypothesis at all.**

## Implementation notes

The two halves of 070S (2) use the site-independent ingredients
`PresheafOfModules.mem_pullbackUnitSubmodule`, `AlgebraicGeometry.span_pullbackSection_eq_top`
and `AlgebraicGeometry.eq_zero_of_mem_span_of_app_eq_pullbackSection`.  The span of the
generators is taken over the `RingCat` object of the structure sheaf on one side and over the
commutative ring `Γ(T, 𝒪_T)` on the other, the two being joined by
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.mem_span_gamma_of_mem_span`; and every equation between sections
is an `Eq.trans` chain rather than a `rewrite`, a motive mentioning a scalar action not being
accepted at the transparency a `rewrite` uses.

The small étale site is a full subcategory cut out by an object property and its topology is
generated by its own covering families, which carry a cardinality bound; the covering by affine
opens is therefore produced by
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.presieve₀_mem_precoverage_of_isOpenImmersion`, which absorbs the
bound through `AlgebraicGeometry.BigEtaleSite.exists_covering_rep`.  This is also why the two
members of each covering family are spelled at the variable morphism
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.openSubHom` rather than through a projection out of the
`CategoryTheory.PreZeroHypercover` structure literal: instance search does not reduce the
projection, so `AlgebraicGeometry.IsOpenImmersion` is not found at that spelling even though it
holds at the first.

Stacks 070S quantifies over the five topologies and over both sites, and 0GN7 and 06VE (1) do
the same, so each statement here is a proper part of its clause.

